DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The functions manage logging of hwpmc(4) events.

     Function ppmmcc__ccoonnffiigguurree__llooggffiillee() is used to turn on and turn off logging.
     If argument _f_d is a valid file handle returned by a prior call to open(2)
     or socket(2) then performance events will be logged to the file corre‐
     sponding to the specified handle.  If the value of argument _f_d is -1 then
     logging will be stopped after any pending data is flushed.

     Function ppmmcc__fflluusshh__llooggffiillee() will force all log data queued inside the
     hwpmc(4) driver to be written out.

     Function ppmmcc__wwrriitteelloogg() will append a log entry containing the value of
     argument _u_s_e_r_d_a_t_a to the log file.

     Function ppmmcc__cclloossee__llooggffiillee() will flush all pending log data and close
     hwpmc(4)'s side of the stream.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Upon successful completion, the value 0 is returned; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     A call to ppmmcc__ccoonnffiigguurree__llooggffiillee() may fail with the following errors:

     [EAGAIN]           The hwpmc(4) driver was not able to create a helper
                        process due to system limits being reached.

     [EBUSY]            Function ppmmcc__ccoonnffiigguurree__llooggffiillee() was called with a log
                        file already configured.

     [EINVAL]           Function ppmmcc__ccoonnffiigguurree__llooggffiillee() was called with an
                        argument of -1 without a log file being previously
                        configured.

     [ENOMEM]           The system encountered a memory shortage when servic‐
                        ing this request.

     A call to ppmmcc__fflluusshh__llooggffiillee() may fail with the following errors:

     [EINVAL]           Function ppmmcc__fflluusshh__llooggffiillee() was called without a log
                        file being previously configured.

     A call to ppmmcc__wwrriitteelloogg() may fail with the following errors:

     [EINVAL]           Function ppmmcc__wwrriitteelloogg() was called without a log file
                        being previously configured.

     [ENOMEM]           The system encountered a memory shortage when servic‐
                        ing this request.

